# 10. RPC vs REST

This is a very important backend comparison.

### REST

You generally think in terms of **resources**:

```http
GET /users/123
```

Conceptually:

> "Give me the user resource."

### RPC

You generally think in terms of **operations/methods**:

```text
GetUser(123)
```

Conceptually:

> "Execute the GetUser operation."

So:

```text
REST
    Resource-oriented

RPC
    Operation-oriented
```

A simplified comparison:

|                    | REST             | RPC                  |
| ------------------ | ---------------- | -------------------- |
| Main idea          | Resources        | Procedures/actions   |
| Example            | `GET /users/123` | `GetUser(123)`       |
| Common transport   | HTTP             | HTTP, TCP, etc.      |
| Data formats       | JSON commonly    | JSON, Protobuf, etc. |
| Coupling           | Usually looser   | Often stronger       |
| Human readability  | High             | Depends              |
| Service-to-service | Very common      | Very common          |
| Typical example    | REST API         | gRPC                 |

But don't think **REST = HTTP** and **RPC = not HTTP**.

For example:

```text
gRPC
  ↓
HTTP/2
```

So RPC can absolutely use HTTP.

