# 12. The biggest problem with RPC

RPC looks like a local function call:

```java
userService.getUser(123);
```

But **it is not a local function call**.

This is one of the most important distributed-systems lessons.

A local call:

```java
getUser(123);
```

might take:

```text
nanoseconds / microseconds
```

A remote call might take:

```text
milliseconds
```

And it can fail because of:

* network failure
* server failure
* timeout
* packet loss
* DNS problems
* overload
* connection problems

Therefore:

> **A remote call is fundamentally different from a local call, even if RPC makes the syntax look similar.**

This is called the **fallacy of distributed computing** territory.

